														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4842600">
									

<p>While this is a little reminiscent of the Sarlacc, the historical value definitely makes it sufficiently unique. There's ony two maor issues:</p>
<p>1) The Foundation wouldn't use more D-Class than needed to verify what it did; while it can be cold, it does try to prevent cruelty, and just keeping it full using D-Class is a waste of resources. At some point they would at least debate substituting cattle or equivalent.</p>
<p>It would be interesting to see if they could feed it just enough to stave off hunger with out increasing its size.</p>
<p>2) Just because it's big doesn't mean that it could be felt using the Richter scale. If it is at the stage where it could be detected using tremors, especially ones that big, then it may be time to debate neutralizing it instead, especially if it is just being kept alive.</p>

							</div>

								
					
